value "images/9c/9cb42cde56fcbea0c489742cab1448890728dab584395129b21794115b1e1298.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386971} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc934043-e8c4-5447-b0e7-d94aa4cef2d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1772040-8608-5c67-8243-2a903b40e108" :question/math-academy-id "q-119383" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](images/9c/9cb42cde56fcbea0c489742cab1448890728dab584395129b21794115b1e1298.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](images/9d/9d256bd6c44a9abc8489c360722b5c5e8243f0d4a9aa6fee03cad52e5334b385.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e1e8df4-9ee7-5f3f-87ce-6b27241b1f47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/58a69833c7b4f627c0cfd436f5ff624ea15dfc0f68d548e94b987794f06a58a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395467} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6eb4ee-97c1-582b-8da7-2c61313e86ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/4191f22560c393dacad29a06e34b7c725800e27554e2c4ad7a9e40d9e56741e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395468} {:answer/id #uuid "0f2fa908-d317-59a8-b3b8-2b0d51743ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e45b8a64f56d831392ddc1eca4ddec922949d58e1c3f1f69c4db6238f